## Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 · **.NET 10** · **Integration test class** (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 3 | 3 |
| Medium | 1 | 1 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

---

### Findings by Severity

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell #1)

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** The `if/else` branch means only one assertion path ever executes per run. If the code unexpectedly returns a `PremiumUser`, the name check is silently skipped (and vice versa).

**Fix:** Split into two deterministic tests:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<User>(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden test gap — one branch is never validated in a given run.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell #4)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Problem:** No assertion. This test passes even if `Insert` silently discards every record. The name implies "no exception = success" but the framework already reports unhandled exceptions as failures — the test adds no value.

**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — 100% pass rate with 0% behavioral verification.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test (Smell #3)

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Problem:** A hard 3-second sleep introduces non-determinism (too short on slow CI, wastes time when fast) and slows the suite unconditionally. Even in integration tests, `Thread.Sleep` is a smell — use a polling/retry mechanism.

**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with timeout instead of fixed sleep
    var timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5);
    var interval = TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(100);
    var sw = Stopwatch.StartNew();

    while (sw.Elapsed < timeout)
    {
        if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
            break;
        await Task.Delay(interval);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        "Notification was not sent within the expected time window.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI; cumulative 3 s wasted on every run.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Catalog)

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Problem:** Four assertions, none with a message parameter. When one fails in CI, the failure output shows a line number but no human-readable context for what expectation was violated.

**Fix — add messages:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist unchanged");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist unchanged");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower triage in CI — developers must open source to identify which property failed.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The following tests are well-structured:

| Test | Why it's clean |
|------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, single behavior focus |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Minimal setup, single assertion on absence |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count `3` is self-documenting (3 inserts above); `CollectionAssert` adds value |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Legitimate async pattern with clear assertion |

The use of in-memory SQLite (`Data Source=:memory:`) is **not** a Mystery Guest — it's hermetic and requires no external state. Good practice for integration tests.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` | ~1 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into 2 focused tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll loop | ~10 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings to assertions | ~2 min |

Fixes 1–2 prevent **false passes** (tests that succeed when they shouldn't). Fix 3 eliminates **flakiness**. Fix 4 improves **diagnosability**.
